  "instance_name": "stereotype_of_young_men_as_unreliable_or_problematic",
  "label": "Stereotype: Young men as unruly, untrustworthy, or socially undesirable",
  "description": "The meme's text, 'if this is what they call pride.. then i don't wanna see what they call shame,' relies on a broader cultural stereotype that associates young men (especially in certain social or racial contexts) with negative traits like recklessness, criminality, or lack of responsibility. This stereotype is used to frame the group's 'pride' as so extreme or offensive that it makes 'shame' seem even more undesirable — a rhetorical device that implies the group is so bad that their 'shame' would be worse. This requires external knowledge of how society often stereotypes young men in this way.",
